  ## `estimateShallowMemoryUsageOf` in `bun:jsc`

  The `estimateShallowMemoryUsageOf` function returns a best-effort estimate of the memory usage of an object in bytes, excluding
  the memory usage of properties or other objects it references. For accurate per-object memory usage, use
  `Bun.generateHeapSnapshot`.

  ```js
  import { estimateShallowMemoryUsageOf } from "bun:jsc";

  const obj = { foo: "bar" };
  const usage = estimateShallowMemoryUsageOf(obj);
  console.log(usage); // => 16

  const buffer = Buffer.alloc(1024 * 1024);
  estimateShallowMemoryUsageOf(buffer);
  // => 1048624

  const req = new Request("https://bun.com");
  estimateShallowMemoryUsageOf(req);
  // => 167

  const array = Array(1024).fill({ a: 1 });
  // Arrays are usually not stored contiguously in memory, so this will not return a useful value (which isn't a bug).
  estimateShallowMemoryUsageOf(array);
  // => 16
  ```


