    // Layout children with new context
    for (const child of element.children) {
      layout(child, childContext);
    }
  }

  3. Intrinsic vs Extrinsic Sizing

  - Intrinsic: "How big do I want to be?" (content-based)
  - Extrinsic: "How big is my container?" (constraint-based)
  - Browsers negotiate between these in multiple passes

  🔄 How Browsers Handle Circular Dependencies:

  Layout Phases:

  1. Min/Max Width Calculation - Bottom-up pass to find intrinsic sizes
  2. Width Resolution - Top-down pass to set actual widths
  3. Height Resolution - Another pass to set heights based on content
  4. Position Resolution - Final pass to set x/y coordinates

