  2. Proxy approach - Intercept property access and convert camelCase to kebab-case
  automatically:
  return new Proxy(styleDeclaration, {
    set(target, prop, value) {
      const kebabProp = camelToKebab(prop);
      target.setProperty(kebabProp, value);
      return true;
    }
  });

  3. Accept the limitation - Document that users should use setProperty() and provide good
  TypeScript types/autocomplete to make it ergonomic.

  Which approach feels right for TTYOM? The hybrid approach might be the sweet spot - common
  properties work intuitively, but we don't have to implement every CSS property that exists.


