> clientLeft, clientHeight, are these viewport properties?


⏺ Yes, clientLeft, clientHeight, clientWidth, and clientTop are viewport/layout properties in
  the DOM. They represent:

  - clientLeft/clientTop - The width of the left/top border of an element
  - clientWidth/clientHeight - The inner width/height of an element (content + padding,
  excluding scrollbars and borders)

  These are part of the Element interface in standard DOM and are used for layout calculations
  and positioning. HappyDOM's Element interface doesn't include these properties, which is why
  we're getting the TypeScript errors - the standard DOM Element type expects these properties
  but HappyDOM's Element doesn't provide them.


